@api = http://localhost:3000/api
@server = http://localhost:3000

### Signup: creates a new account and stores the user in the database.
### Use this first so you have a real user for signin and user lookup tests.
POST {{api}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Test ",
    "email": "test1@example.com",
    "password": "password1234"
}

### Signin: verifies the email and password, then returns a JWT token.
### Copy the `token` value from the response if you want to test protected routes.
POST {{server}}/auth/signin
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "test+rest@example.com",
    "password": "password123"
}

### Invalid signin: shows the error response when the password is wrong.
### This confirms the backend rejects incorrect credentials.
POST {{server}}/auth/signin
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "test+rest@example.com",
    "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### Signout: clears the auth cookie so the current session is logged out.
GET {{server}}/auth/signout

### List users: returns all saved users with basic fields only.
### Use this to confirm the signup request worked and to copy a real user id.
GET {{api}}/users

### Read user: fetches one user by id.
### Replace `USER_ID` with an id from the list users response.
@USER_ID = replace_with_user_id
GET {{api}}/users/{{USER_ID}}

### Protected example: sends a Bearer token to a route that requires authentication.
### This is a pattern example only; it works only if your backend exposes `/api/protected`.
GET {{server}}/api/protected
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN_HERE

### =========================
### Contacts
### =========================

### Create contact: adds a new contact record.
POST {{api}}/contacts
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "firstname": "Jane",
    "lastname": "Doe",
    "email": "jane.doe@example.com"
}

### Invalid create contact: missing required fields should return a validation error.
POST {{api}}/contacts
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "firstname": "NoEmail"
}

### List contacts: returns all saved contacts (firstname, lastname, email only).
### Use this to copy a real contact id for the read/update/delete requests below.
GET {{api}}/contacts

### Read contact: fetches one contact by id.
### Replace `CONTACT_ID` with an id from the list contacts response.
@CONTACT_ID = 6a454d2931396c7097a41aed
GET {{api}}/contacts/{{CONTACT_ID}}

### Update contact: updates fields on an existing contact.
PUT {{api}}/contacts/{{CONTACT_ID}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "lastname": "Smith"
}

### Delete contact: removes a single contact by id.
DELETE {{api}}/contacts/{{CONTACT_ID}}

### Delete all contacts: clears the contacts collection.
DELETE {{api}}/contacts

### =========================
### Education (Qualifications)
### =========================

### Create qualification: adds a new education record.
POST {{api}}/qualifications
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "BSc Computer Science",
    "firstname": "Jane",
    "lastname": "Doe",
    "email": "jane.doe@example.com",
    "completion": "2020-06-01",
    "description": "Graduated with honors"
}

### Invalid create qualification: missing required fields should return a validation error.
POST {{api}}/qualifications
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "Missing required fields"
}

### List qualifications: returns all saved education records.
### Use this to copy a real qualification id for the read/update/delete requests below.
GET {{api}}/qualifications

### Read qualification: fetches one qualification by id.
### Replace `QUALIFICATION_ID` with an id from the list qualifications response.
@QUALIFICATION_ID = replace_with_qualification_id
GET {{api}}/qualifications/{{QUALIFICATION_ID}}

### Update qualification: updates fields on an existing qualification.
PUT {{api}}/qualifications/{{QUALIFICATION_ID}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "description": "Updated description"
}

### Delete qualification: removes a single qualification by id.
DELETE {{api}}/qualifications/{{QUALIFICATION_ID}}

### Delete all qualifications: clears the qualifications collection.
DELETE {{api}}/qualifications

### =========================
### Projects
### =========================

### Create project: adds a new project record.
POST {{api}}/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "Portfolio Website",
    "firstname": "Jane",
    "lastname": "Doe",
    "email": "jane.doe@example.com",
    "completion": "2024-01-15",
    "description": "Personal portfolio built with MERN"
}

### Invalid create project: missing required fields should return a validation error.
POST {{api}}/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "Missing required fields"
}

### List projects: returns all saved projects.
### Use this to copy a real project id for the read/update/delete requests below.
GET {{api}}/projects

### Read project: fetches one project by id.
### Replace `PROJECT_ID` with an id from the list projects response.
@PROJECT_ID = replace_with_project_id
GET {{api}}/projects/{{PROJECT_ID}}

### Update project: updates fields on an existing project.
PUT {{api}}/projects/{{PROJECT_ID}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "description": "Updated description"
}

### Delete project: removes a single project by id.
DELETE {{api}}/projects/{{PROJECT_ID}}

### Delete all projects: clears the projects collection.
DELETE {{api}}/projects

### Notes:
### - `{{server}}` points at the auth routes and root server endpoints.
### - `{{api}}` points at the user, contact, qualification, and project CRUD routes.
### - Replace `TOKEN_HERE` with the JWT returned by signin.
### - Replace `USER_ID` / `CONTACT_ID` / `QUALIFICATION_ID` / `PROJECT_ID` with actual ids from their respective list requests.
### - Make sure the server is running on localhost:3000 (npm start / node server.js) before running these requests.